                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/269: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-24T16:00:00-03:00">November 24, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 24—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. The Foreign Office today urgently requested me to obtain at the earliest
                    possible moment the Department’s reply to my 173, November 23, 1 p.m., stating
                    that it is most anxious to sign the agreement with Germany this week.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office informs me that it has secured the consent of the Germans to
                    omit from the agreement the point treated in the Department’s 76, November 13,
                    10 a.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
